.TH RESONATE-CONFIG.TOML 5 "" "resonate" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
resonate-config.toml \- the settings file of resonate(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/resonate/config.toml
.br
.I \-\-config FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The settings file is TOML.
A key that is absent takes its default, a command-line flag naming the same setting wins over the
file for one run, and a key that is not listed below is ignored with a warning.
A value that will not read costs its own key alone: the key stays at its default, a warning says
which, and every other key is read.
A file that is not valid TOML is refused.
.PP
The window and several subcommands write this file back (the settings pane, resonate\-eq, the
sign-ins).
They edit it in place, so comments and the order of keys survive, and they leave the file readable
by its owner alone, since it can hold secrets.
A running window or player reads the file once, when it starts: a change made to the file, or by a
subcommand, is heard by the next start.
.PP
A path is a string.
Blank is the same as absent, and a leading
.B ~
is the home folder.
A key marked
.B secret
is never printed in a log or by the debug output.
Every request resonate makes says only
.IR resonate/<version> ,
and a contact, a key or a token is sent only where it is typed into this file.
.SH AUDIO OUTPUT
.TP
.B sink
String. The node.name of the PipeWire sink to play to. Default: the graph's default sink.
.TP
.B quality
String: fast, balanced, high or very-high. The resampler's quality. Default: high.
.TP
.B filter-phase
String: linear, intermediate or minimum. The resampler filter's phase. Linear rings before a
transient as well as after it, minimum only after it. Default: linear.
.TP
.B true-peak
Boolean. Weigh the true peak of what the equaliser adds, so a boost is held under full scale rather
than reaching the hard clamp. Default: true.
.TP
.B restore-lossy
String: off, repair or extend. Repair the damage an MP3, AAC or Vorbis encoder leaves under its
cutoff, or repair and rebuild the treble it cut away above it. Default: off.
.TP
.B dither
String: none, rectangular or triangular. The dither covering a word length the output is too short
to hold. Default: triangular.
.TP
.B noise-shaping
String: flat, lipshitz or threshold. The curve the dither noise is shaped by. Default: threshold.
.TP
.B replay-gain
String: off, track or album. Which ReplayGain tags level the volume. Default: off.
.TP
.B replay-gain-pre-amp
Number of decibels, from \-20 to 20. Added to every level ReplayGain sets. Default: 0.
.TP
.B replay-gain-untagged
Number of decibels, from \-20 to 20. Applied to a track that carries no ReplayGain tags. Default: 0.
.TP
.B bit-perfect
Boolean. Switch the graph to the source's rate when it can, instead of resampling to the rate it
already runs at. Default: true.
.TP
.B force-graph-rate
Boolean. Make the graph run at the rate chosen rather than leave it to the other clients on it.
Default: true.
.TP
.B dop
Boolean. Hand DSD to the device as DoP; off, it is decimated to PCM. Default: false.
.TP
.B dsd-like-pcm
Boolean. Decimate DSD to the level of PCM; off, a DSD master plays some 6 dB quieter than the same
music in PCM. Default: false.
.TP
.B device-volume
Boolean. Turn the device's own volume where it has one; off, the samples are scaled. Default: false.
.TP
.B volume
Number from 0 to 1. The volume playback starts at. Default: 1.
.TP
.B buffer-ms
Integer of milliseconds. How much audio is kept buffered ahead of the device. Default: 500.
.TP
.B bluetooth-wake
Boolean. Keep Bluetooth headphones from cutting the start of the music: a paused device is woken
ahead of it. Default: false.
.TP
.B bluetooth-lead-ms
Integer of milliseconds, from 0 to 5000. How long before the music a Bluetooth device is woken.
Default: 750.
.TP
.B bluetooth-awake-s
Integer of seconds, from 0 to 10800. How long a paused Bluetooth device is held awake. Default: 300.
.TP
.B skip-repeats-queue
Boolean. Next, under repeat of the track, repeats the queue; off, it keeps repeating the track.
Default: true.
.TP
.B previous-restarts
Boolean. Previous restarts the track playing once it is more than three seconds in; off, it
always goes back a row.
Default: true.
.SH EQUALISER
.TP
.B equaliser
Boolean. Whether the equaliser is on. Default: false.
.TP
.B equaliser-profile
String or true. The kept profile every device without one of its own uses, or true for the device's
own curve. Default: none.
.TP
.B equaliser-for
Table. Maps a sink's node.name to the profile it uses, or to true for its own curve. A binding that
names neither is ignored with a warning. Default: empty.
.TP
.B equaliser-measurer
String. The measurer whose AutoEq correction is preferred where several measured a device, for
resonate\-eq \-\-find and \-\-suggest (which \-\-measurer outranks) and the pane's suggestions.
A device it did not measure keeps the usual ranking. Default: none.
.TP
.B equaliser-measurer-for
Table. Maps a sink's node.name to the measurer preferred for that device alone, in place of
equaliser\-measurer. Default: empty.
.TP
.B convolution
Path. An impulse response convolved with the signal, for room correction. Default: none.
.SH LIBRARY AND FILES
.TP
.B library
Path. The library database. Default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/resonate/library.db.
.TP
.B vault
Path. The managed vault, opened on the next start, which must exist. Default: none; a vault is made
only where resonate\-vault is asked to.
.TP
.B inbox
Path. A folder whose songs resonate treats as a provider and offers to wants. Default: none.
.TP
.B music-folder
Path. The one ordinary folder new songs are copied into. Default: none.
.TP
.B file-dropped
Boolean. File a song dropped on the window into the music folder by organise-as. Default: true.
.TP
.B organise-as
String. The layout that files a song, from the fields {albumartist}, {artist}, {album}, {title},
{year}, {disc}, {track} and {ext}, separated by /.
Default: {albumartist}/{album}/{disc}{track} {title}.
.TP
.B music-extensions
Array of strings. The audio extensions listings include, case-insensitive, with or without the dot.
Absent is every extension the build scans, empty is none. Default: absent.
.TP
.B minimum-length-s
Integer of seconds, from 0 to 600. Listings leave out a song shorter than this. Default: 0.
.TP
.B history-kept
String forever, or a whole number of days. Listens and skipped time older than this are forgotten on
each start. Default: forever.
.TP
.B resume
Boolean. Start again with the queue, and the place in the song, that was left. Default: true.
.SH ONLINE
.TP
.B online
Boolean. False stops every network request. Default: true.
.TP
.B enrich-after-scan
Boolean. Ask the reference about albums and artists once a scan has finished. Default: true.
.TP
.B study
Boolean. Study each track a lookup finds: its spectrum, loudness and print. Default: true.
.TP
.B fetch-lyrics
Boolean. Ask LRCLIB for the lyrics of a track as it plays. Default: true.
.TP
.B lyrics-language-from-locale
Boolean. Choose among lyric sheets named by language by the locale. Default: false.
.TP
.B identify-by-sound
Boolean. Let a lookup recognise a track by its sound when its tags name nothing. Default: false.
.TP
.B contact
String, secret. A contact address sent with requests to services that ask for one. Default: none.
.TP
.B hosted-services
Boolean. Let a blank or absent hifi-api and monochrome fall back to the hosted services. Default:
true.
.TP
.B acoustid-key
String, secret. An AcoustID application key. Default: none.
.TP
.B audd-token
String, secret. An AudD token. Default: none.
.TP
.B listenbrainz-token
String, secret. A ListenBrainz token that scrobbles what is heard. Default: none.
.TP
.B lastfm-key
String, secret. The key of a Last.fm API account registered by the listener. Default: none.
.TP
.B lastfm-secret
String, secret. The shared secret of that account. Default: none.
.TP
.B lastfm-session
String, secret. The session resonate\-lastfm writes. All three Last.fm keys are needed before
anything is scrobbled. Default: none.
.TP
.B listen-from
String: desktop, microphone, or a node.name. What resonate\-listen listens to. Default: desktop.
.TP
.B listen-for
Integer of seconds, from 4 to 60. How long it listens for. Default: 12.
.SH SOURCES
.TP
.B subsonic
String. The address of a Subsonic server. Default: none.
.TP
.B subsonic-user
String. The Subsonic account. Default: none.
.TP
.B subsonic-password
String, secret. The Subsonic account's password. Default: none.
.TP
.B tidal-client-id
String. The client TIDAL's sign-in needs. Default: none.
.TP
.B tidal-client-secret
String, secret. That client's secret. Default: none.
.TP
.B tidal-refresh-token
String, secret. Written by resonate\-tidal, and rewritten when TIDAL rotates it. Default: none.
.TP
.B hifi-api
String. The address of a TIDAL-compatible server of the listener's. Default: none.
.TP
.B hifi-secret
String, secret. A key the Resonate server at https://resonate.tecnio.dev lists. While set, wanted
songs are also asked of that server, as a provider of its own beside hifi-api and whatever hifi-api
and hosted-services say, with the key as a bearer token. The key is sent to that server alone, over
https. Default: none.
.TP
.B monochrome
String. The address of a Monochrome server of the listener's. Default: none.
.SH DEVICES
.TP
.B sync
Boolean. Keep devices in step. Off whenever online is off, unless sync-nearby-only is on.
Default: true.
.TP
.B sync-nearby-only
Boolean. Use no server: devices sync only on the same network. Default: false.
.TP
.B sync-server
String. The sync server's address. Blank is the hosted server. A \fBws://\fR or \fBwss://\fR address
reaches the server over a WebSocket, which a proxy such as Cloudflare carries. Default: blank.
.TP
.B sync-server-certificate
Path. A PEM certificate trusted beside the system roots, for a server of the listener's. Default:
none.
.TP
.B sync-stun
String. A STUN server (\fBhost\fR or \fBhost:port\fR, port 3478 by default) that tells this device
its public address, which it hands to other devices to connect directly. Needed to reach devices
through a server that is only reachable over a WebSocket. Blank asks none. Default: blank.
.TP
.B sync-key
String, secret. The pairing code, minted and written on the first start that syncs. Default: none.
.TP
.B sync-device
String. The name other devices see. Default: Linux.
.TP
.B sync-songs
Array of strings: favourites, playlists, everything. Which songs travel to other devices without
being asked for; empty is only on request. Default: empty.
.TP
.B discord
Boolean. Tell Discord what is playing. Default: false.
.TP
.B discord-app
String of 17 to 20 digits. The Discord application id; nothing is shown without it. Default: none.
.TP
.B discord-shows
String: application, track or album. How much of what is playing is said. Default: album.
.TP
.B discord-art
String: cover, icon or none. The picture shown. Default: cover.
.TP
.B discord-icon
String. The name of the asset shown as the icon. Default: none.
.TP
.B discord-progress
Boolean. Show how far into the track it is. Default: true.
.TP
.B discord-paused
Boolean. Keep showing the track while it is paused. Default: false.
.SH WINDOW
.TP
.B theme
String: resonate, midnight, graphite, amoled, plum, rose-pine, rose-pine-moon, catppuccin-mocha,
catppuccin-macchiato, catppuccin-frappe, nord, gruvbox-dark, tokyo-night, dracula, one-dark or
solarized-dark. Default: resonate.
.TP
.B accent
String: mauve, blue, teal, green, amber, peach or red. The accent colour. Default: the theme's own.
.TP
.B text-size
String: small, medium or large. Default: medium.
.TP
.B notify
Boolean. Raise a desktop notification when the track changes. Default: true.
.TP
.B minimise-button
Boolean. Draw the window's minimise button. Default: true.
.TP
.B maximise-button
Boolean. Draw the window's maximise button. Default: true.
.TP
.B scroll-volume
Boolean. The wheel over the player changes the volume. Default: true.
.TP
.B mouse-navigation
Boolean. The mouse's back and forward buttons navigate. Default: true.
.TP
.B scrollbars
String: shown, auto-hide or hidden. A boolean still reads, true as shown and false as hidden.
Default: auto-hide.
.TP
.B artists-drawn
String: grid or list. Default: grid.
.TP
.B spectrum-tilt
String: flat, pink or steep. The spectrum's slope in decibels per octave. Default: pink.
.TP
.B spectrum-floor
String: 60, 78 or 96, in decibels under full scale. Default: 78.
.TP
.B spectrum-bands
String: thirds, sixths or twelfths of an octave. Default: sixths.
.TP
.B spectrum-falls
String: slowly, middling or quickly. How fast the bars fall back. Default: middling.
.TP
.B suggestions-tab
Boolean. Show the Suggestions tab. Default: true.
.TP
.B missing-tab
Boolean. Show the Missing tab. Default: false.
.TP
.B tab-counts
Boolean. Count the rows beside each tab's name. Default: false.
.TP
.B remember-tab
Boolean. Open on the tab last used; off, last-tab is removed. Default: true.
.TP
.B last-tab
String naming a tab: albums, artists, tracks, statistics, queue, playlists, favourites,
suggestions, missing, lyrics, inspector, visualiser, analysis or settings. Written by the window.
.TP
.B remember-window-size
Boolean. Open at the size last used; off, window-size is removed. Default: true.
.TP
.B window-size
String WIDTHxHEIGHT in pixels, from 720x520 to 8192x8192. Written by the window.
.TP
.B remember-settings-category
Boolean. Open settings on the category last used; off, last-settings-category is removed.
Default: true.
.TP
.B last-settings-category
String: output, processing, equaliser, library, filters, online, sync, desktop, appearance or
about. Written by the window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/resonate/config.toml
The settings file.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/resonate/
The library, the vault, the kept equaliser profiles and the sync ledger.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR resonate (1)
